        "kind": "none",
        "exposedClass": "informational",
        "statement": "Existing policies keep nested variable substitution unless they adopt the new notation; using `{{- ... }}` limits substitution to one pass so Kyverno does not attempt to resolve `{{ }}` content inside the substituted data (e.g. an HCL string from a ConfigMap).",
        "remediation": "Where substituted rule data contains `{{ }}` that Kyverno must not resolve, use the `{{- ... }}` declaration (e.g. `{{- hcl }}`) for shallow substitution.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      "statement": "Kyverno 1.13.0 adds a `{{- ... }}` notation for shallow (one-time) variable substitution, letting a policy substitute rule data (e.g. an HCL string defined in a ConfigMap) without Kyverno attempting to resolve the nested `{{ }}` variables inside it."
    },
